Text:
The Reconciliator makes the desk start one fearlessOnClick when a person opens a file with one of some extensions.
A 'program' is named by the TaggedText that encodes the path of that program.
os.holders is a Holders: (OSExtension->TaggedText) is in os.holders exactly while the desk starts the program TaggedText when a person opens a file with the extension OSExtension, for example with a double click.
os.holders holds every program of the desk that the desk starts in that way.
The desk, a person and every program can change os.holders at any moment.
reconciliator$reconcile only adds to os.holders: an extension that was in OSExtensions at one call and is not at the next call keeps its Holder.
A program is 'a fearlessOnClick' when the last segment of the path of that program is the file name of fearlessOnClick.
//later: how the person is asked to let a fearlessOnClick open the files of an extension, and which program shows that question
//later: what the Reconciliator writes on each desk, and how the Reconciliator reads os.holders on each desk
//later: the icons that the desk shows for the files of an extension and for the windows of a program
//later: two calls of reconciliator$reconcile never run at the same time on one desk

Grammar:
OSExtensions ::= OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn
FearlessExtension ::= "fearless" | "fapp" [0-9][0-9][0-9] | "ffile" [0-9][0-9][0-9]
Holders ::= Holder1 .. Holdern
Holder ::= (OSExtension->TaggedText)

Well formedness:
in OSExtensions: if OSExtensions is OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn, then OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn are disjoint
in Holders: if Holders is (OSExtension1->_) .. (OSExtensionn->_), then OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn are disjoint

Signature: reconciliator$personAllows(OSExtension,TaggedText)//holds when the person, asked, lets a fearlessOnClick open the files with the extension OSExtension in place of the program TaggedText

Signature: reconciliator$allowed(OSExtensions) = OSExtensions'//the extensions of OSExtensions that a fearlessOnClick can take

Define OSExtension in reconciliator$allowed(OSExtensions):
A fact OSExtension in OSExtensions
B fact (OSExtension->_) not in os.holders

Define OSExtension in reconciliator$allowed(OSExtensions):
A fact OSExtension in OSExtensions
B fact (OSExtension->TaggedText) in os.holders
C fact TaggedText is a fearlessOnClick.

Define OSExtension in reconciliator$allowed(OSExtensions):
A fact OSExtension in OSExtensions
B fact (OSExtension->TaggedText) in os.holders
C fact TaggedText is not a fearlessOnClick.
D fact OSExtension is of form FearlessExtension.

Define OSExtension in reconciliator$allowed(OSExtensions):
A fact OSExtension in OSExtensions
B fact (OSExtension->TaggedText) in os.holders
C fact TaggedText is not a fearlessOnClick.
D fact OSExtension is not of form FearlessExtension.
E fact reconciliator$personAllows(OSExtension,TaggedText)

Signature: reconciliator$reconcile(TaggedText,OSExtensions) = OSExtensions'//TaggedText is a fearlessOnClick; OSExtensions' are the extensions of OSExtensions that the desk now starts TaggedText for

Define reconciliator$reconcile(TaggedText,OSExtensions):
A fact reconciliator$allowed(OSExtensions) = OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn
B action the desk is changed so that (OSExtension1->TaggedText) .. (OSExtensionn->TaggedText) are in os.holders
C if OSExtensioni is of form FearlessExtension and (OSExtensioni->TaggedText) is not in os.holders, error reconciliatorErrorFearlessExtensionIsNotHeld(OSExtensioni)
D action return OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn

Implementation notes:
Another program can undo the change of line B at once. The implementation does line B a few times before line C.
